Z||000003||FieroPerformance||09-12-2001||04:53 PM||||BlackDragon<P>     I am not sure if they offer roller rockers for the 4 cyl. fieros. I know that they are rare and expensive for the V6. If you are going to get high compression pistons you will also have to have machine work done on your block... not cheap at all. Just the machine work on my 2.8 is going to cost close to $750. If you want more performance look into a v8 or v6 swap... they aren't cheap but they will definitly give you more bang for your buck than pistons or rockers.<P>just my 2 cents (i dont even know if I am right about the rocker arms)<P>-Charlie<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Cooter||09-12-2001||06:04 PM||||The Duke already uses a high ratio rocker, like a 1.7 big block rocker arm. You might could modify a set of 1.8 Harland Sharpe's to fit. I had a set on my big block suburban and they are more cost effective than most other brands.||||reg||1
